issue.body:
Empty conditions for `matching()` are causing `null` to be passed to `QueryAssociation::_addConditions()`, resulting in an error as an array is being expected.

> Argument 1 passed to Cake\Database\Expression\QueryExpression::_addConditions() must be of the type array, null given, called in \src\Database\Expression\QueryExpression.php on line 124

Here's a test case that triggers the error:

``` php
public function test7099()
{
    $table = TableRegistry::get('articles');
    $table->belongsToMany('tags');

    $table
        ->find()
        ->matching('tags', function ($q) {
            return $q->where([]);
        })
        ->all();
}
```

The `null` value stems from the dummy query, where `clause()` will return the default value, which is `null`.

**https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0.10/src/ORM/Association.php#L545-L549**

Refs #7099
